  "raw_response": "Looking at the examples, I can identify the rule:\n1. Find the non-zero pattern and its horizontal period\n2. Create a reflected copy (vertically flipped + column phase shift) extended by the period\n3. Place both copies in the grid with symmetric gaps\n\nThe column shift is determined by auto-correlation of row-to-row transitions within the pattern.\n\n```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    R = len(grid)\n    C = len(grid[0])\n    cells = [(r, c) for r in range(R) for c in range(C) if grid[r][c] != 0]\n    if not cells:\n        return [row[:] for row in grid]\n    color = grid[cells[0][0]][cells[0][1]]\n    min_r = min(r for r, c in cells)\n    max_r = max(r for r, c in cells)\n    h = max_r - min_r + 1\n    pattern = [set() for _ in range(h)]\n    for r, c in cells:\n        pattern[r - min_r].add(c)\n    P = C\n    for p in range(1, C + 1):\n        ok = True\n        for row in pattern:\n            if not row:\n                continue\n            groups = {}\n            for c in row:\n                groups.setdefault(c % p, []).append(c)\n            for cols in groups.values():\n                cols_s = sorted(cols)\n                for i in range(len(cols_s) - 1):\n                    if cols_s[i + 1] - cols_s[i] != p:\n                        ok = False\n                        break\n                if not ok:\n                    break\n            if not ok:\n                break\n        if ok:\n            P = p\n            break\n    templates = [set(c % P for c in row) for row in pattern]\n    best_s, best_score = 0, -1\n    for s in range(P):\n        score = 0\n        for i in range(h - 1):\n            shifted = set((c + s) % P for c in templates[i])\n            score += len(shifted & templates[i + 1])\n        if score > best_score or (score == best_score and s < best_s):\n            best_s, best_score = s, score\n    s = best_s\n    total_gap = R - 2 * h\n    gap = max(total_gap // 2, 0)\n    original_center = (min_r + max_r) / 2.0\n    grid_center = (R - 1) / 2.0\n    output = [[0] * C for _ in range(R)]\n    def place_original(start):\n        for i in range(h):\n            for c in pattern[i]:\n                if 0 <= start + i < R:\n                    output[start + i][c] = color\n    def place_reflected(start):\n        for i in range(h):\n            src = templates[h - 1 - i]\n            shifted = set((c + s) % P for c in src)\n            for c in range(C):\n                if c % P in shifted and 0 <= start + i < R:\n                    output[start + i][c] = color\n    if original_center <= grid_center:\n        r1 = max(min(min_r, R - 2 * h - gap), 0)\n        r2 = r1 + h + gap\n        place_original(r1)\n        place_reflected(r2)\n    else:\n        r2_start = max(min_r, h + gap)\n        r2_start = min(r2_start, R - h)\n        r1 = max(r2_start - h - gap, 0)\n        r2 = r1 + h + gap\n        place_original(r2)\n        place_reflected(r1)\n    return output\n```",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    R = len(grid)\n    C = len(grid[0])\n    cells = [(r, c) for r in range(R) for c in range(C) if grid[r][c] != 0]\n    if not cells:\n        return [row[:] for row in grid]\n    color = grid[cells[0][0]][cells[0][1]]\n    min_r = min(r for r, c in cells)\n    max_r = max(r for r, c in cells)\n    h = max_r - min_r + 1\n    pattern = [set() for _ in range(h)]\n    for r, c in cells:\n        pattern[r - min_r].add(c)\n    P = C\n    for p in range(1, C + 1):\n        ok = True\n        for row in pattern:\n            if not row:\n                continue\n            groups = {}\n            for c in row:\n                groups.setdefault(c % p, []).append(c)\n            for cols in groups.values():\n                cols_s = sorted(cols)\n                for i in range(len(cols_s) - 1):\n                    if cols_s[i + 1] - cols_s[i] != p:\n                        ok = False\n                        break\n                if not ok:\n                    break\n            if not ok:\n                break\n        if ok:\n            P = p\n            break\n    templates = [set(c % P for c in row) for row in pattern]\n    best_s, best_score = 0, -1\n    for s in range(P):\n        score = 0\n        for i in range(h - 1):\n            shifted = set((c + s) % P for c in templates[i])\n            score += len(shifted & templates[i + 1])\n        if score > best_score or (score == best_score and s < best_s):\n            best_s, best_score = s, score\n    s = best_s\n    total_gap = R - 2 * h\n    gap = max(total_gap // 2, 0)\n    original_center = (min_r + max_r) / 2.0\n    grid_center = (R - 1) / 2.0\n    output = [[0] * C for _ in range(R)]\n    def place_original(start):\n        for i in range(h):\n            for c in pattern[i]:\n                if 0 <= start + i < R:\n                    output[start + i][c] = color\n    def place_reflected(start):\n        for i in range(h):\n            src = templates[h - 1 - i]\n            shifted = set((c + s) % P for c in src)\n            for c in range(C):\n                if c % P in shifted and 0 <= start + i < R:\n                    output[start + i][c] = color\n    if original_center <= grid_center:\n        r1 = max(min(min_r, R - 2 * h - gap), 0)\n        r2 = r1 + h + gap\n        place_original(r1)\n        place_reflected(r2)\n    else:\n        r2_start = max(min_r, h + gap)\n        r2_start = min(r2_start, R - h)\n        r1 = max(r2_start - h - gap, 0)\n        r2 = r1 + h + gap\n        place_original(r2)\n        place_reflected(r1)\n    return output",
